# Borrow validation

Roots, joins, optional transfer safety and facts.

## Contract

- Input: validated HIR, access/effect metadata, and external boundary classifications
- Output: normalised semantic places and overlap facts, value origins and preliminary provenance, shared and exclusive access liveness, path-sensitive future-use and last-use classifications, optional affine-transfer candidates, capable-source-death and temporary-borrow-safety proofs, preliminary return-root alias and projection evidence, reactive invalidation facts, and resolved external access-boundary classifications
- Decides: shared/exclusive conflicts and whether transfer is safe as an optimisation
- Must not decide: lifetime topology, physical ownership, final allocation, or backend lowering
- Invariant: borrow validation reads HIR and writes side tables; it doesn't rewrite HIR

This output contract is solver-independent. The current alpha lattice, root approximation and advisory drop candidates are current scaffolding rather than permanent architecture; a stronger production borrow checker may replace them without changing the contract or source legality.

A future checked proof-budget proposal may let selected lexical scopes authorise substantially deeper conflict-directed analysis. It would preserve the same safety contract and ordinary fast path. It is not accepted syntax or current production behaviour.

